            <ArticleTitle>Transient posterior knee pain with the meniscal arrow.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>762-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 31% incidence of focal posterior knee pain was noted in our initial experience with all-inside meniscal repair using the absorbable Meniscal Arrow system (Bioscience, Tampere, Finland). The pain was transient, resolved by 6 months in all cases, and was unrelated to the length of implant. A typical case is presented to assist surgeons in counseling patients who experience transient posterior knee pain after meniscal repair with this system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
